o Shia Iran, and the Turkish/ Syrian border region where ISIS is a daily presence. She then returns to Europe, first in London, where she uncovers the identity of the notorious ISIS executioner \"Jihadi John,\" and then in Paris and Brussels, where terror has come to the heart of Western civilization.","publicationYear":2017,"displaySummary":"The daughter of a Turkish mother and a Moroccan father, she was born and educated in Germany and has worked for several American newspapers. Since the 9/11 attacks she has reported stories among the most dangerous members of her religion; when she is told to come alone to an interview, she never knows what awaits at her destination. In this compelling and evocative book, Mekhennet seeks to answer the question, \"What is in the minds of these young jihadists, and how can we understand and defuse it?\" She has unique and exclusive access into the world of jihad and sometimes her reporting has put her life in danger. We accompany her from Germany to the heart of the Muslim world -- from the Middle East to North Africa, from Sunni Pakistan to Shia Iran, and the Turkish/ Syrian border region where ISIS is a daily presence. She then returns to Europe, first in London, where she uncovers the identity of the notorious ISIS executioner \"Jihadi John,\" and then in Paris and Brussels, where terror has come to the heart of Western civilization.","primaryTopic":"Immigration, Refugees & Borderlands","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Memoir & Autobiography","mappedSubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book is primarily a personal narrative reflecting Souad Mekhennet's experiences as a journalist navigating and reporting on jihadism, thus qualifying it as Memoir & Autobiography, while also encompassing 